course: dictionary
lesson: 3735
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Put your bag on the floor» means the flat surface of a room that you walk on.
explain: «The office is on the third floor» means a level of a building, one above another. The clue is the word building, and the number tells you which level. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "the third level of the building" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: «The ocean floor» means the ground at the bottom of the sea. Here the clue is ocean, which is water, so the floor must be underneath it. When you meet a word with several meanings, ask: what is the topic, and which meaning fits here?
fact: Floor means the flat part of a room that you walk on.
fact: Floor also means a level of a building, such as «the third floor».
fact: Floor can mean the ground at the bottom of the sea or a forest, as in «the ocean floor» or «the forest floor».
fact: In Britain, the «ground floor» is the level at street level; in the US, this same level is called the «first floor».
fact: «Floored» can mean knocked down, or surprised very much.
exercise: «Keep toys off the floor, so nobody trips over them.» What does floor mean here? | The level of a building | *The flat surface of a room that you walk on | A bag for carrying shopping | The ground at the bottom of the sea
exercise: «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» Where does this activity happen? | *At the bottom of the sea | Inside a bus | In a shop | On the top of a mountain
exercise: In Britain, «ground floor» means the floor at street level. What is this same level called in the US? | Roof | Second floor | *First floor | Basement
test: «In a flood, move up to higher floors.» What does floors mean here? | Flat surfaces you walk on, like carpet | The ground at the bottom of a river | Tiles you cover a wall with | *Levels of a building, one above another
test: «Her friend stared at the floor and would not talk.» What does this tell us? | Her friend was asleep | She was counting the floors of a building | Her friend was dancing | *Her friend was looking down, possibly upset or hiding a problem
exam: A floor is 4 metres long and 3 metres wide. What is its area in square metres? | 24 | *12 | 7 | 14
